            "review_title": "Review at Tri Hang Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Ringo Wong\nHong Kong, China84 contributions\n0\nTrue local seafood restaurant\nJan 2018 • Couples\nIn a quiet street a few minutes walk from the rong bridge (head), here lays a \"not-so-nice-looking\" restuarent where local people coming frolicking and enjoying seafood. This is Tri Hang.\nIt doesn't have breath taking view, nor offering any 5 stars environment or facility. But it does serve some truely, locally tasted seafood with super reasonable price. Foods are freshly prepared and are of high quality with no doubt. The only downside is that their staffs can communicate only with very limited English, nor do they offer an English menu. But they can show you photos of their foods with their cellphones so you can pick from them or also you can show them photos of foods you want and ask for them. This is truly authentic! \nThis restaurant is truly a hidden 💎 in Da Nang.\nRead more\nWritten January 15, 2018",
